abstract: >-
  MELITE is an open-source Python package for the evaluation and selection
  of supervised classification and regression models using numeric tabular
  datasets. It supports classification-only, regression-only, and mixed-task
  workflows.

  Model evaluation uses task-specific cross-validation strategies and
  selection criteria: F1-macro for classification and RMSE for regression.
  Supported models are optimized with Optuna when hyperparameter tuning
  is applicable. Evaluation results, optimization summaries, and provenance
  are preserved in task-specific artifacts.

  Selected models can be fitted on the full dataset, exported, and reused
  for prediction. The resulting evaluation evidence supports reproducible
  model comparison but does not establish external predictive
  generalizability.

keywords:
